WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.666 --> 00:00:07.041
- Trans athletes and allies are fighting a surge of
proposed anti-transgender legislation across the U.S.

00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:13.458
Many of these bills have aimed to ban trans athletes from
competing on teams that affirm their gender identities. 

00:00:13.458 --> 00:00:17.041
Trans girls and trans women
are the main targets of these bills,

00:00:17.041 --> 00:00:21.666
with backers believing they have an unfair
advantage over cisgender competitors,

00:00:21.666 --> 00:00:25.291
but trans rights advocates say
it's not about wins and losses.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:28.708
Lindsay Hecox’s dream of running
cross-country for Boise State

00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:33.916
was put on hold when Idaho passed
House Bill 500 in the spring of 2020.

00:00:33.916 --> 00:00:39.583
Billie Jean King, Candace Parker, Megan Rapinoe
and almost 200 other athletes signed

00:00:39.583 --> 00:00:44.375
an amicus brief speaking out against the law,
which has since been suspended.

00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:49.041
This isn’t the first time the sports world has
pushed back against anti-trans legislation.

00:00:49.041 --> 00:00:55.000
In 2016, the NBA and NCAA pulled
major events out of North Carolina

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.583
in response to a bill prohibiting trans people from
using public restrooms that matched their identities.

00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:04.375
This contributed to the law's partial repeal in 2017.

00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:10.083
But athletes like CeCé Telfer, the first out
trans woman to win an NCAA title,

00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:14.166
want to see the organization take a
firmer stance on current legislation.

00:01:14.166 --> 00:01:20.458
- As a trans athlete, first of all, I am not a threat
to women's sports because I am a woman.

00:01:20.458 --> 00:01:25.416
- The NCAA has since stated host sites
must be "free of discrimination."

00:01:25.416 --> 00:01:29.250
Trans students will also now be
protected under Title IX.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.000
The surge of legislation is unprecedented,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.458
but discrimination against trans, non-binary
and intersex people is not new.

00:01:37.458 --> 00:01:43.083
Pride Month historically celebrates
and honors LGBTQ+ communities,

00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:47.958
but activism against anti-trans legislation
reminds us of where Pride began:

00:01:47.958 --> 00:01:54.916
in struggle and for visibility,
power, solidarity and equality.

